# Dev server (Edgeways)

Sam needs continual localhost uptime. Treat the running Next server as sacred.

## Do

- If nothing listens on `:3000`, start with `npm run dev:detached` from `edgeways/`
  (supervised, survives agent-shell cleanup). Confirm with a quick curl.
- Prefer reading `edgeways/data/dev-keep.pid` / `dev-keep.log` over restarting.
- Leave a healthy server alone while you edit code (HMR handles it).

## Do not

- Do **not** `pkill -f "next"` / `pkill -f "next dev"` / kill listeners on 3000
  unless Sam explicitly asked you to restart the server.
- Do **not** `rm -rf edgeways/.next` while a server is running (causes ENOENT
  storms and dead pages).
- Do **not** start a second `npm run dev` that steals another port (3001…).
- Do **not** rely on an agent background shell as the long-lived server; use
  `dev:detached` or tell Sam to run `npm run dev` in their own terminal.

## Why the site dies after ~15 minutes

Next.js 16 exits the worker when heap crosses ~80% (`Server is approaching the
used memory threshold, restarting…`). That is normal. Downtime happens when the
**parent process tree** is gone (agent shell abort, blanket pkill). The keep
supervisor in `edgeways/scripts/dev-keep.mjs` exists to bring it back.